==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{label|en|countable|mostly in|botany}} The wood from any conifer (or from ''[[Ginkgo]]''), without regarding how soft this wood is.
#: ''SYP is a '''softwood''', but it is harder than many hardwoods.''
# {{label|en|countable}} (in more general use) As the preceding but limited to those that are commercial timbers.
# {{label|en|countable|forestry}} The tree or tree species that yields the preceding
#: ''This '''softwood''' has been planted extensively throughout Scotland.''
# {{label|en|uncountable}} A joint term for the commercial timbers, without distinguishing which.
#: ''You should have used '''softwood''' for the frame of this shed, instead of overbuilding it like this.''

